<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <POU Name="FB_TimeStampBuffer" Id="{b2db97ec-7312-4822-a3b4-76ec1968b59f}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_TimeStampBuffer
(*
    Companion to FB_LREALBuffer: accumulates one wall-clock timestamp per sample.

    Purpose:
        Samples the PLC's Unix time on every cycle where bExecute is TRUE and
        collects the samples into a fixed-size block, so that a consumer can
        retrieve a whole block of timestamps in a single read. Drive it from the
        same bExecute as a FB_LREALBuffer instance to obtain a matched pair of a
        value block and a timestamp block.

    Usage:
        Call the block once per PLC cycle - not conditionally - so that the
        internal buffer index stays in step with the samples taken:

            fbTimeStamps : FB_TimeStampBuffer;

            fbTimeStamps(bExecute := bAcquire);

        While bNewArray is FALSE, arrOutput holds the last completed block and
        may be read at any time. bNewArray pulses TRUE for a single cycle when a
        new block has been copied into arrOutput; a consumer that must see every
        block latches its copy on that edge.

    Objectives:
        - Fill the timestamp block without ever blocking the PLC cycle: each call
          stores at most one sample.
        - Keep the output interface identical to FB_LREALBuffer so that the value
          block and the timestamp block line up element for element.
        - Report readiness explicitly via bNewArray instead of requiring the
          consumer to track the sample count itself.

    History:
        2019-10-09 Zachary Lentz  - Original version.
        2026-11-27 Audit finding  - Completed the header (usage/objectives/
                                    history) and documented arrOutput and
                                    bNewArray.
*)
VAR_INPUT
    // If TRUE, we'll accumulate a value on this cycle.
    bExecute: BOOL;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
    // Block of the 1000 most recently collected timestamps, in units of seconds
    // since 1970-01-01 00:00:00 UTC (Unix time; fractional part is milliseconds).
    // Refreshed as a whole only once the block has been filled; between
    // refreshes it still holds the previously completed block.
    arrOutput: ARRAY [1..1000] OF LREAL;
    // TRUE for exactly one cycle, on the cycle where a full block of 1000
    // timestamps has been copied into arrOutput. FALSE at all other times.
    bNewArray: BOOL;
END_VAR
VAR
    fbUnixTime: FB_UnixTimestamp;
    fbLREALBuffer: FB_LREALBuffer;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[fbUnixTime(
    bExecute := bExecute,
    fTime => fbLREALBuffer.fInput);
fbLREALBuffer(
    bExecute := bExecute,
    arrOutput => arrOutput,
    bNewArray => bNewArray);]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>